Dismiss image updates

POST /api/updates/dismiss takes {"image": "<image>"} or {"all": true},
forgets those updates (saved to updates.json) and answers with the new list.
It needs a session and JSON like the other settings endpoints, is refused
with 403 in read-only mode, answers 400 for any other body and 404 when the
server keeps no updates. An unknown image is a no-op, so a double click or
two open tabs never errors.

